	(footprint "rp2040_midi_bridge:USB_A_Neltron_5075AR-04-WH"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "7d8e4171-de1f-4fe2-b8b1-6ab8604c3a4a")
		(at 29 31.1 180)
		(descr "USB-A female THT receptacle, Neltron 5075AR-04-WH (Akizuki tsuhan-code 100160). Signal pads: 4x dia0.92mm round PTH, pitch 2.50/2.00/2.50mm (pin1=VBUS pin2=D- pin3=D+ pin4=GND). Shell mounting pegs (pin 5/6): 2x dia2.3mm PTH, pad dia2.8mm, 13.14mm apart, offset 2.70mm toward the board side (local +Y) from the signal row -- inward of the signal row, away from the mating opening. The manufacturer PCB layout places the 2-ø2.3 holes 2.70mm on the signal-row side opposite the opening -- brass/nickel-plated per datasheet, soldered for mechanical strength and tied to GND on the PCB (net assigned directly on the board instance, not via the schematic symbol, same convention as J1/J3's unused header pins beyond the symbol's pin count). Body width ref 15.80mm (F.SilkS outline widened to 16.3mm 2026-08-22, see note below; the 15.80mm figure remains the true datasheet body dimension). Source: manufacturer drawing (2026-08-19). PTH CONVERSION 2026-08-22: shell pegs changed NPTH->PTH, pad dia 2.3mm(=drill, 0 annular ring)->2.8mm (requested range 2.8-3.0mm; chose the low end since the pad now pokes past the 15.80mm-wide body-reference silk outline at the pin's 13.14mm span -- 2.8mm pokes ~0.07mm, 3.0mm would poke ~0.17mm). The F.SilkS side edges were widened from +-7.9mm to +-8.15mm to clear kicad-cli DRC's silk_over_copper (silkscreen clipped by solder mask) warning that the poke-through caused; this only stretches the reference outline, it does not change the real pin/pad geometry or the datasheet body width. SHELL PEG SIDE: the two ø2.3mm shell holes stay 2.70mm on the mating-opening side of the signal row, matching the completed carrier board. Place J2 so the opening face sits at the board edge; with the board bottom edge at +Y, the placement is rotated 180 degrees.")
		(tags "USB-A THT connector host")
		(property "Reference" "J2"
			(at 0 -8 180)
			(layer "F.SilkS")
			(uuid "72f95a9d-c865-4bf9-a2c4-51f27d39373f")
